    fix(backtrack): retain capture-aware continuations

    Use ordered heap continuation tasks for ECMAScript backreference searches. Preserve distinct capture states at equal endpoints, group modifier rollback, repeat clearing/progress and atomic forward/reverse assertions. Accept empty matches that the continuation has fully validated. Report terminal match-capture allocation failures through the existing per-search error boundary.

    Node-derived 4,144-row comparisons improve 612 value/capture and 666 capture-index mismatches to zero, with no new mismatches in the measured matrix. Twenty-two focused tests pass, including exhaustive search-allocation fault injection, real search recovery and bounded positive/negative/reverse exhaustion. Final frozen-source Debug gate passes 49/49 steps and 645/645 tests in 508.616 seconds. Initial empty-match and OOM gaps were reproduced and retained before the final fixes. Non-ECMAScript matching, static critical-pattern guards and default resource limits remain unchanged. Engine/test262 impact will be measured through the immutable consumer pin; no complete tokenizer or package compatibility claim.

